 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Report Automation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is report automation?\", \"a\": \"Report automation is software that produces a recurring report without anyone assembling it by hand. It pulls figures from the systems that hold them, runs the math, tests the results against your rules, and delivers the report on a schedule.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you set up automated reporting?\", \"a\": \"Start with one recurring report and list each figure with the system it comes from. Describe that report and who reads it to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>. It connects each source and writes the checks that hold a report back when a number looks wrong. Leave reports that change shape every month for later.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should automated reporting for clients include?\", \"a\": \"A client report should carry the few metrics the client pays you to move, the same figures for the prior period, and a short note from the account manager on what changed. Keep the send date fixed each month. Automated reporting for clients can also give each client a login to check the numbers between sends. Turning each report into a branded file is <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/document-automation'>document automation</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is automated financial reporting software used for?\", \"a\": \"Finance teams use it to produce the month-end pack without rebuilding it in spreadsheets: the income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow statement, plus budget against actual by line. Automated financial reporting software reads the closed figures straight from the accounting system. Sign-off on the pack before it reaches the board is an approval workflow.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between report automation and dashboard automation?\", \"a\": \"Report automation produces a fixed report on a schedule and sends it to people, often after someone signs off. Dashboard automation keeps a screen of metrics current, refreshing each tile from its source for anyone to check at any hour. Many teams run both on the same data: the dashboard for daily checks, the report as the record of what was said.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the benefits of automated reporting?\", \"a\": \"Figures arrive on schedule and come straight from the source systems, not from a copy of last month's spreadsheet. Analysts stop rebuilding the same report, and pasting errors stop reaching readers. Every sent version is kept, which shows what a reader was told and when. An app built on Emergent runs each scheduled report with no task cap, however often it fires.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some automated reporting examples?\", \"a\": \"Any report that keeps the same shape each period is a candidate: a weekly sales pipeline review, a support backlog by queue, stock below its reorder point, or site traffic by channel. Pipeline reviews read from the CRM, and keeping that CRM current is the job of <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/sales-automation'>sales automation</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you use AI in automated reporting?\", \"a\": \"AI helps in two places. It can draft the plain-English summary above the numbers, and it can read figures out of documents that have no API, such as a supplier statement sent by email. Keep the arithmetic in ordinary calculations, and have a person compare any number the summary quotes with the table before the report goes out.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best report automation tools?\", \"a\": \"Most fall into two groups. BI platforms such as Power BI refresh dashboards and email scheduled snapshots to subscribers. Integration platforms move data between apps and can post a result to Slack. Emergent takes a third route and writes the reporting app itself from a prompt, hold rules and send times included.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you make sure automated reporting is accurate?\", \"a\": \"Reconcile it to a number you already trust. Each run should compare at least one total with a second system, such as booked revenue in the CRM against invoiced revenue in accounting, and log how many rows it pulled from each source. A sudden drop in rows usually means a broken connection, not a slow week.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
